Separate packet admission, retained history and visible publication. Bind admitted decoding to its originating file and attempt; retain its history effect on completion even after cancellation, hiding, replacement or disposal. Original src/progress.js: "    const deliver = frame => { record(frame); receive(frame); };" README.md: "`recordProgress` appends transfer history. `showProgress` paints the panel." Recheck visit authority after recording because host callbacks may navigate synchronously. Original src/queue.js: "      if (state.current === visit) state.showProgress({ fileId: visit.file.id, attemptId, frame });" Cancellation of an attempt alone does not revoke presentation of already admitted decoding while its visit remains current and its frame remains eligible.

Coordinate cleanup ownership across synchronous startup, listener removal and cancellation. Retire captured ownership before releasing resources; after callbacks return, verify that an older operation cannot overwrite newer navigation. Original src/panel.js: "  const previous = state.current;
  state.current = null;
  if (previous) releaseVisit(previous);
  if (state.disposed || state.nextVisit !== requestId) return null;" Preserve removal commitment and repeated-removal behavior. src/progress-source.js: "// Removal commits before notifying the host. The host callback is synchronous
// and may call workspace.select(...) or workspace.hide(). Repeated removal is inert." Preserve abort, progress cleanup and cancellation notification order from src/transfer.js: "  controller.signal.addEventListener("abort", () => {
    stopProgress();
    onCancel({ file, attemptId, signal: controller.signal });
  }, { once: true });" Reconcile resources returned after retirement without replacing newer ownership.

Keep an accepted retry bound to its entry visit and file across cancellation callbacks. Cancel the previous attempt before enqueueing; preserve the accepted retry's record and transfer construction even if cancellation navigates; cancel the resulting retired handle and suppress its queued notice. Original src/retry.js: "  const previous = visit.handle;
  previous.cancel();
  const handle = enqueueTransfer(state, visit, "retry");
  if (state.current === visit) visit.handle = handle;
  else handle.cancel();
  if (state.current === visit) publishQueued(state, visit, handle);" Preserve queue recording before transfer construction, independent workspace counters and idempotent disposal. src/queue.js: "// Queue records are retained even when their originating panel visit ends."

Separate admission, retained audit and visible delivery. Capture originating file and attempt identity for admitted decoding. Preserve audit once at completion even after cancellation, retirement or disposal; then check originating visit authority before visible publication. README.md: "Every accepted progress event is recorded exactly once when decoding
finishes, including work accepted before the visit closes." README.md: "Removing a listener does not retract a decode
that already started. Closing or replacing the visit stops visible progress;
new visits remain live." Original src/progress.js: "    const deliver = frame => { record(frame); receive(frame); };" Original src/queue.js: "      if (state.current === visit) state.showProgress({ fileId: visit.file.id, attemptId, frame });" Preserve this visit-based publication check: attempt cancellation alone does not revoke visible delivery of previously admitted decoding while its visit remains current. Reopening the identical file creates a different visit and does not authorize old results to paint it.

Coordinate cleanup ownership before synchronous startup can navigate. Make retirement prevent new admission immediately, reconcile resources returned after retirement, and prevent resumed older work from overwriting newer ownership. README.md: "`showProgress` may synchronously select or hide through
the workspace, and normal current progress must remain visible." Retire captured panel ownership before canceling it, and recheck navigation identity afterward. Original src/panel.js: "  const previous = state.current;
  state.current = null;
  if (previous) releaseVisit(previous);
  if (state.disposed || state.nextVisit !== requestId) return null;" README.md: "Selection and hiding may themselves cancel an old handle and synchronously
receive newer navigation; the newer navigation keeps ownership." Preserve native cancellation and cleanup-before-notification ordering. Original src/transfer.js: "  controller.signal.addEventListener("abort", () => {
    stopProgress();
    onCancel({ file, attemptId, signal: controller.signal });
  }, { once: true });" Preserve idempotence and independent workspace disposal. README.md: "Disposal removes subscriptions and cancels transfers; work already accepted
for audit remains retained."

Bind accepted retries to their entry file and visit across cancellation reentry. Cancel the previous attempt before enqueueing, retain exactly one accepted command and queue record even if cancellation navigates, cancel its resulting transfer if retired, and suppress its retired queued notice. README.md: "The accepted old retry must still enqueue and record once after such navigation.
Its newly created transfer is canceled immediately if its visit has ended; this
does not remove its retained queue record." Original src/retry.js: "  const previous = visit.handle;
  previous.cancel();
  const handle = enqueueTransfer(state, visit, "retry");
  if (state.current === visit) visit.handle = handle;
  else handle.cancel();
  if (state.current === visit) publishQueued(state, visit, handle);" Preserve record-before-transfer construction and independent counters. Original src/queue.js: "  const attemptId = ++state.nextAttempt;
  state.record(makeQueueRecord(visit.file, attemptId, visit.id, kind));"

Enqueue the latest accepted text using the existing trailing-task utility with a 120 ms quiet interval. Bind delayed persistence to the document accepting the edit rather than resolving a later selection. Preserve empty text, later bursts, and no-selection editing as a no-op. Original src/editor.js contains "if (current) store.write(current.id, text);"; src/trailing-task.js contains "      pending = args;
      handle = timers.schedule(flush, delay);". These sources do not require a separate in-memory text model or reusable document buffer bank.

Retire consumed pending arguments and timer ownership before invoking callback-capable persistence. Preserve src/trailing-task.js ordering: "    handle = null;
    const args = pending;
    pending = null;
    if (args !== null) work(...args);" Nested flushing must not consume the same batch twice, and completion cleanup must not erase a batch enqueued by a subscriber.

Capture departing resources, revoke current ownership, stop the captured status subscription, and complete old-view clearing before flushing pending persistence, or guard remaining effects against successor navigation. Flush before reading a replacement document. Original src/editor.js contains "    const leaving = current;
    current = null;
    if (leaving) leaving.stop();
    renderDocument(null);" and "      renderDocument({ id, text: store.read(id) });". Together with README.md's "its last accepted edit", the original immediate write supports synchronous departure flushing across switch, same-document reopen, close, and disposal.

Stopping a subscription must also revoke delivery by a callback already captured in an ongoing notification snapshot. src/draft-store.js contains "      for (const listener of [...listeners]) listener(event);" and "      return () => listeners.delete(listener);"; removing Set membership cannot remove a callback from that existing array. README.md requires "they stop when that view begins closing." Retain document filtering from src/save-status.js, "    if (event.id === id) renderStatus(event);", while adding a view-local delivery guard that is revoked before unsubscribing.

After departure saving invokes subscribers, ensure an outer open continuation does not overwrite a successor opened or closed during that save. Protect clearing effects as well as destination installation; captured departing cleanup must not affect successor resources or pending edits. src/draft-store.js establishes the callback boundary with "      records.set(id, text);
      const event = { id, text };
      for (const listener of [...listeners]) listener(event);". A navigation generation check is one implementation strategy for preserving ownership across the newly introduced departure save, not evidence of a universal navigation precedence contract.

